deploy_gate:
  instruction: Before deploying TinyRustLM.MiRust.com or TinyRustLM.com, update this developer portal, MiRust.com, MiniModel.org, and any remaining SLMComposer.com redirect/public export surfaces to match the deployed source behavior.
  requirements:
    - Keep source options, .slm verification claims, model documentation, and no-server-model-byte boundaries current.
    - Document Hugging Face metadata/conversion handoffs, local MiniModel share metadata export, and known-peer MiniModel serve/fetch handoffs when TinyRustLM app behavior changes; do not imply broad P2P discovery, relays, or project-hosted model bytes until implemented.
    - Keep TinyRustLM.com documented as the root app route; do not describe /app/ as the canonical TinyRustLM.com path.
    - Keep the former standalone runtime documentation lane documented only as retired/preserved content under /docs/runtime-portal/.
    - Keep SLMComposer.com documented only as a retired or redirecting app identity, not the canonical public app.
    - Run relevant pointer audits and git diff --check before packaging or deployment.
required_private_read_order:
  - workspace.uai
  - .uai/index.uai
  - .uai/totem.uai
  - .uai/taboo.uai
  - .uai/talisman.uai
  - .uai/file-handoff.uai
  - .uai/intake-outcome-ledger.uai
  - .uai/short-term-memory.uai
current_state:
  - TinyRustLM.MiRust.com is the TinyRustLM developer portal.
  - TinyRustLM.com is the root-domain browser-local Rust/WASM app route.
  - Hugging Face search rows in TinyRustLM are metadata until MiniModel metadata names an admitted .slm with peer-offer proof or the user locally converts source bytes with Rust and imports a verified .slm.
  - TinyRustLM's simple Hugging Face lane defaults P2P on, shows P2P Import only for MiniModel matches with write-catalog-entry peer-offer proof, shows Start Conversion otherwise, and shows one list-level warning when P2P is disabled.
  - Proof-ready MiniModel rows use metadata-only catalog entries with peer_hint_status=peer-offer-ready-known-peer-needed and peer_import_status=request-script-ready; P2P Import still requires the list-level Known peer URL, rejects project/Hugging Face hosts, and uses local Rust `import-peer-request` receiver execution for fetch, assembly, verification, and import receipt before browser import.
  - TinyRustLM can save local MiniModel share metadata after verified .slm import; MiniModel can export/serve/fetch/reassemble known-peer pieces, while broader peer discovery/relay remains later.
  - The former standalone runtime documentation corpus was preserved under docs/runtime-portal/ with a checksum manifest while its separate documentation authority is retired.
  - SLMComposer.com is no longer the canonical public app identity.
  - The live public-safe export is verified.
  - Direct public .uai and agent-file-handoff access is denied.
